{
  "_note": "Default Earth-reference thresholds. Applied AFTER the personal-baseline check (microgravity rule 1). EVERY value is a configurable default that MUST be reviewed by a flight surgeon before any operational use. Rules are evaluated red first, then yellow, else green. Operators: lt, le, gt, ge.",
  "_review_status": "REVIEW NEEDED – not approved by a flight surgeon",
  "baseline": {
    "sd_multiplier": 2.0,
    "min_points": 5,
    "window_days": 7,
    "citation": [
      "hrp_oi_2015",
      "nasa_cv_risk"
    ],
    "rationale": "Personal baseline first. In 0 g the reference is the astronaut's own EARLY-FLIGHT readings (first 7 days in 0 g, after the ~2 L headward fluid shift); in 1 g / partial g it is the PRE-FLIGHT baseline. Outside mean ± 2 SD = 'differs from your baseline'.",
    "soften_yellow_within_baseline": true,
    "_soften_note": "If a value is inside the personal baseline band, an Earth-range YELLOW is shown as GREEN with a note (avoids false alarms from expected 0 g shifts). RED is NEVER softened."
  },
